<?nvs
// The file that does not compile, which two of this tier's surfaces need one of.
//
// `nvs run` over it exits non-zero having printed one diagnostic in the renderer's own format, which is
// what the `$nvs` problemMatcher parses into a Problems entry — the Task being useful rather than
// decorative is `rule:ide/tasks-carry-a-problem-matcher`, and only a real failing run shows it. The AST
// panel opens on the same file for the opposite reason: `nvs ast --json` is resilient by default, so a
// file with an error in it is the one that proves the panel draws the tree the parser recovered
// (`rule:ide/the-ast-panel-shells-out-to-the-cli`).
//
// The error is a name nothing declares, which the resolver reports as `E0301` after the file has parsed.
// That is why it is a name error and not a syntax error: the tree stays a whole one, so the two
// assertions read the same fixture instead of wanting two.

int $count = 2 + 3;

echo $count + $missing, "\n";
